{
  "description": "This protocol is part 4 of a 4-part protocol designed to accomplish the Sample-Barcoding Module of the plexWell 384 Low Pass Library Preparation.\nPart 1\nPart 2\nPart 3\nPart 4\nThis protocol performs the second half of Step 3 (SB Pooling). During this protocol, each column of the destination plate in Part 3 is pooled into a 2mL DNA LoBind tube. The user has the option to pool up to 12 columns (the entire plate) into individual tubes for each column.\n\n\n\nOpentrons P300 Single Channel Pipette (GEN2)\nBio-Rad 96-Well Plate, 200µL PCR, containing samples from Part 3\nOpentrons 200µL Filter Tips\nOpentrons 24 Tube Rack\n2mL DNA LoBind Tubes\n\n\n\nSlot 1: Opentrons 200µL Filter Tips\nSlot 2: Empty\nSlot 3: Bio-Rad Plate, containing samples\nSlot 4: Empty\nSlot 5: Empty\nSlot 6: Tube Rack with 2mL Tubes",
  "tags": [
    "NGS Library Prep",
    "plexWell LP384"
  ],
